                <pb facs="0524" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg510"/>

                <head>
                    <seg type="margin">[156]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">*Mr. McCulloch, collector, to Mr. Lowry, surveyor.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,
                            Baltimore</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1824-08-09"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">August</hi> 9, 1824</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Please to send two inspectors of the
                    customs to-morrow morning to examine the Colombian cruiser Aguila, below the
                    fort. The object is to ascertain that no addition is made to her force by any
                    new warlike equipments or enlistments of American seamen. In case such should
                    appear, you will direct the officers to detain the commission, &amp;c., of the
                    vessel herewith sent and immediately report it here. If otherwise, they will
                    deliver the captain his papers, and if the cutter can be found, deliver Captain
                    Webster the letter handed herewith. Return if no occasion requires a further
                    proceeding. But if the cutter is not to be seen, it will be proper for an
                    officer to go on till she can be met with or any other public vessel, to the
                    commander of which the letter to Captain Webster may then be delivered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. H. McCULLOCH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Lowry</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Surveyor of the Port of Baltimore.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
